course: dictionary
lesson: 12194
title: Keeping secrets safe
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Confidentiality means keeping private information secret. Information that is confidential is only shared with people who are allowed to know it. «The nurse kept my test results confidential.» The nurse told nobody else, not even my friends.
explain: Look inside the word: confidentiality comes from confide, which means to trust someone with a secret. «Please tell me in confidence.» When someone asks for something to be kept in confidence, they are trusting you to keep it private.
explain: Some secrets must be told. A counsellor keeps your worries private, but if someone might be in danger, the adult must tell people who can help, even if you asked them not to. Confidentiality protects you, but it never means hiding a danger.
fact: Confidentiality is a noun, and it is uncountable: you say «confidentiality», not «confidentialities».
fact: «Confidentiality» means keeping private information secret and only sharing it with people who are allowed to know it.
fact: Doctors, lawyers and counsellors have a duty of confidentiality, so they must keep private information private.
fact: «Patient confidentiality» means a doctor keeps a patient's health information private.
fact: School staff keep things private, but if a child might be in danger, they must tell people who can help.
exercise: «The school nurse kept my worry private. She promised to keep it in confidence.» What does «in confidence» mean? | Read out loud in assembly | *Kept private, only for people who are allowed to know | Shared with the whole class | Forgotten the next day
exercise: Which word means keeping private information secret? | Punctuality | *Confidentiality | Curiosity | Celebration
exercise: «Ella's bank has a confidentiality agreement with her.» What does this suggest? | The bank is closed on Sundays | The bank will lose her money | *The bank must keep her details private | The bank will share her details with everyone
test: «The counsellor said, "What you tell me stays confidential, unless someone could be hurt."» What does confidential mean here? | Written on the board | Shown on television | Loud and clear | *Kept private and secret
test: Which of these is an example of confidentiality? | Sending a letter to the newspaper | *Keeping your friend's private news to yourself | Writing your friend's name on the board | Telling the whole school what your friend said
exam: Which sentence shows confidentiality? | «The bank posted my details online.» | *«The doctor keeps my test results private.» | «The nurse put my name on the notice board.» | «The doctor shared my test results with the whole class.»
